{
  "instance_id": "bottlepy__bottle.a8dfef30.func_basic__f94rj5df",
  "repo": "swesmith/bottlepy__bottle.a8dfef30",
  "problem_statement": "Route.reset() clears entire __dict__ breaking plugin functionality\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen `Route.reset()` is called, it now clears the entire `__dict__` instead of just removing the 'call' key. This breaks plugin functionality because plugins may store important attributes on the route object that get wiped out.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport bottle\n\nclass TestPlugin(object):\n    def apply(self, callback, route):\n        # Plugin stores something on the route\n        route.plugin_data = \"important_data\"\n        return callback\n\napp = bottle.Bottle()\napp.install(TestPlugin())\n\n@app.route('/')\ndef hello():\n    return \"Hello World\"\n\n# Get the route object\nroute = app.routes[0]\n\n# Plugin data should be there\nprint(\"Before reset:\", getattr(route, 'plugin_data', 'MISSING'))\n\n# Reset the route (this happens internally)\nroute.reset()\n\n# Plugin data is now gone\nprint(\"After reset:\", getattr(route, 'plugin_data', 'MISSING'))\n```\n\nExpected output:\n```\nBefore reset: important_data\nAfter reset: important_data\n```\n\nActual output:\n```\nBefore reset: important_data\nAfter reset: MISSING\n```\n\nThe issue affects any plugin that stores state on route objects, causing them to lose their configuration or cached data when routes are reset.",
